1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,874
The pistol shrimp knocks out fish with
a claw that never even touches them.

2
00:00:05,167 --> 00:00:05,663
Instead,

3
00:00:05,663 --> 00:00:10,748
it snaps the claw so fast that the jet of
water it shoots out tears open a bubble.

4
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:15,793
Then the bubble collapses with a crack
loud enough to stun or even kill a small

5
00:00:15,793 --> 00:00:16,093
fish.

6
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,205
And as it collapses,
it even flashes with light,

7
00:00:19,205 --> 00:00:23,704
which means that for an instant it's
nearly as hot as the surface of the Sun.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,808
So when thousands of
these shrimp snap at once,

9
00:00:26,808 --> 00:00:31,529
their crackle can drown out navy sonar,
which really happened in World War Two.
